														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1452577">
									

<p>This is one of those that I wrote a while back and left in my sandbox. But it was one that got some better responses, so I dusted it off, tweaked it up a bit, and posted it.</p>
<p>The idea here is that you can't know which version is more accurate. The researcher in the second one, Dr. Carter, is supposed to be a generally jaded sort of fellow, used to examining dark eldritch horrors all day, and he's excited to find something that's anomalous but&#8230;pleasant. But the Foundation isn't in the practice of just accepting the idea that an SCP can be beneficial (since they usually aren't, even when they seem to be). So I leave it up to you to decide which version you think is the truth.</p>

							</div>

								
					
