					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/anaxagoras" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1019930); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1019930&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607936274" alt="Anaxagoras" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1019930)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/anaxagoras" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1019930); return false;" >Anaxagoras</a></span> <span class="odate time_1337352144 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">18 May 2012 14:42</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1452641">
									

<p>This doesn't work for me. There is literally no reason the Foundation would lie about something like this. There's lots of SCPs that are perfectly safe to be around. If the Foundation doesn't want this thing used by dying Foundation personnel, then they just forbid that. Lying about the object's properties serves no real purpose, and actually imperils personnel by giving them incomplete relevant information.</p>
<p>Also, a 50km radius is gigantic, especially in a relatively densely populated area like the US. You can't just make a region that big disappear. That's almost four times larger than the largest county in Kentucky. That's pretty ridiculous.</p>

							</div>

								
