														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1452648">
									

<p>It's more the attitude the Foundation displays towards the SCP than towards people approaching it. The original researcher believed the entity had an essentially beneficial nature, and wrote a containment document that reflected that. The rewritten version presumes that the object is dangerous and writes a document accordingly. The issue is that between the two versions, you can't know what the actual object does; the article is (in addition to presenting the SCP) intended to show the level of discretion that different researchers or policymakers have in how containment is handled. Moreover, it's possible that the first version is actually correct and the second version was written by someone with mental instability brought on by exposure to the SCP.</p>
<p>Also, neither version really imperils personnel; the containment procedures are basically &quot;get away from this if you want to live.&quot; The first version just makes that a lot stricter.</p>

